History of SQL
1. SQL was introduced by Raymond Francis Boyce and Donald Chamberlin in 1970’s.
2. In previous days, SQL was known as SEQUEL (SIMPLE ENGLISH QUERY LANGUAGE)
3. In 1986, ANSI (AMERICAN NATIONAL STANDARD INSTITUTE) changed the name from SEQUEL to SQL due to trademark conflicts.

What is SQL?
SQL stands for Structured Query Language (or) Sequential Query Language which is used to interact with the Database.

