SUBQUERY: “A query written inside another query is known as 
                           subquery.”

WORKING PRINCIPLE:
	
    

          INPUT										
						DEPENDENT

                                                                                                             
                         	OUTPUT



Let us consider two queries i.e., outer query and inner query.
•	Inner query is also known as subquery.
•	Always inner query will produce output first.
•	The output of inner query will be the input to an outer query.
•	The outer query will execute and generate the final RESULT.
•	So, we can say that outer query is dependent on the inner query.

WHEN / WHY DO WE USE SUBQUERY: 
CASE 1: “Whenever there is unknown present in the question we have to use subquery, to identify the unknown.”
CASE 2: “Whenever the data to be select and condition to be executed present in different tables than we can use subquery case2.”

NOTE:
1.In the Inner Query / Sub Query we cannot select more than One column.

2.The corresponding columns need not be same, but the datatypes of those have to  
    be same.
